Request: Email the AP lead a list of all unpaid bills with their amounts and due dates.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Email the AP lead a list of all unpaid bills with their amounts and due dates.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants a single email sent from the AP shared mailbox to the accounts-payable lead containing a complete, accurate list of every 
currently unpaid bill in the ERP, with each bill's amount and due date.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A sent email (visible in the AP mailbox Sent folder, sent to the AP lead's address) listing every unpaid bill with its amount and due date 
— or, if no unpaid bills exist, a sent email stating that — plus confirmation of the recipient used and the count of bills reported; if the AP lead's address 
cannot be determined, a report back to the user instead of a guess.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - ERP access for this task is read-only: do not record, edit, delete, or re-status any bill, vendor, or payment.
  - No emails may be sent other than the single report email to the AP lead.
  - Only bills whose status is 'unpaid' in the ERP are included; do not silently drop or add bills in other statuses (paid, partial, draft, void).
  - Amounts and due dates in the email must be copied verbatim from ERP bill records, not recalculated or reformatted in a way that changes their value.
  - The email must be sent from the AP shared mailbox (ap@kestrel.in).
  - If the AP lead's email address cannot be determined from company systems, do not guess — stop and report back to the requester.
  - Do not invent bill ids, amounts, or due dates; every value must come from a real ERP lookup.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Every bill the ERP reports as status='unpaid' at the time of sending is represented in the sent email (set equality, not just a count match), or — if the 
ERP reports zero unpaid bills — the email explicitly states there are no unpaid bills.
  C2. For each reported bill, the amount and due date in the email match the corresponding ERP bill record exactly (bill id / invoice number, amount, due date).
  C3. Exactly one new email exists in the AP mailbox Sent folder, addressed to the AP lead's address, with the required list content; no duplicate or extra 
messages were sent.
  C4. No unintended changes were made: bill statuses, bill records, vendors, and payment schedules in the ERP are identical before and after the task (no new 
bills, no status changes, no scheduled payments).
  C5. Exception branch honored: if the AP lead's email address cannot be resolved from company systems, no report email was sent and the requester instead 
received a statement of the blocker and the candidate addresses found.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The ERP's 'unpaid' status is the authoritative definition of an unpaid bill for this request.
  - The AP shared mailbox ap@kestrel.in is the correct sending identity for reports to the AP lead.
  - Currency and date values will be shown as recorded in the ERP (with currency label), without conversion.
  - Today's date (2026-10-10) is the as-of date for the 'unpaid' snapshot.
  - If the ERP returns zero unpaid bills, a report email stating that is still the desired deliverable rather than silence.
PLAN:
  S1: Log into the ERP (read-only) and retrieve the complete list of bills with status='unpaid', capturing bill id, invoice number, vendor, amount, and due date
for each. (done when: A concrete list of unpaid bills with amounts and due dates exists, plus a pre-task snapshot of all bill statuses for later comparison.)
  S2: Determine the AP lead's email address from company systems (mailbox contacts/threads, signatures, or any directory visible in the mail or ERP systems), 
resolving to a single unambiguous recipient. (done when: One confirmed email address for the AP lead is identified and its source is recorded, or a clear 
statement that no unambiguous candidate could be found.)
  S3: Compose the report email from ap@kestrel.in to the AP lead listing each unpaid bill with its amount and due date (and identifying fields such as 
bill/invoice id and vendor for clarity), then send it. (Sending is approval-gated by policy; the platform will request approval on the send action.) (done when:
The email is sent and appears in the Sent folder with content matching S1's data.)
  S4: Verify the outcome: re-check the Sent folder for the single message and re-query the ERP to confirm no bill/status/payment changes were made. (done when: 
C1–C4 (or the C5 exception branch) are confirmed against live system state.)
